   [EnableIf=is_android]
   LocateViews(gfx.mojom.Rect element_window_rect, float virtual_display_height)
       => (array<DisplayXRRigView> views);
+
+  // browser#128 (M3): the true on-screen frame of the browser's content area
+  // (android.R.id.content), absolute screen device px, plus its display id.
+  // Replaces the GPU provider's (0,0) placeholder origin, which anchored the
+  // interlace phase at the panel origin — correct only for a bottom-anchored
+  // full-width window, and measured wrong for everything else (a freeform
+  // window at (2137,84) wove with its phase referenced ~2137 px away).
+  // Sent by the browser process's Choreographer-cadence sampler
+  // (DisplayXrWindowGeometry.java): change-gated with a ~1 s heartbeat, so a
+  // GPU restart or a pure window MOVE (which raises no resize) self-heals
+  // within a second. Per ADR-033 this reports geometry and NOTHING else; the
+  // weaver alone owns phase and snapping.
+  // |container_scaled| (option 1, detect-and-don't-weave): true when the
+  // window's bounds exceed the display's maximum metrics — the app-visible
+  // tell of an OEM freeform "mini window" whose whole surface is scaled for
+  // display (measured 0.67x on NP02J). A woven texture resampled by any
+  // factor is destroyed, so the GPU provider refuses to weave while set and
+  // the page's own 2D content shows instead.
